    closing: {
        heading: 'What I actually think',
        body: [
            'If the Committee gave me capital for this sector today, I would put the great majority of it into six names and treat the rest as watchlist or research overhead.',
            'The core would be **Ipca, Ajanta, Corona Remedies and Caplin Point**, with **RPG** and **Jagsonpal** as the smaller-cap expression of the same idea. Every one of them earns above 17% on capital, sells brands rather than molecules, and is levered to the part of the cycle that is currently working. Ipca is the safest entry at 36x with guidance raised mid-year. Caplin is the one I think is genuinely mispriced — 31.6x for a 34.9% margin business with a logistics moat in Latin America and ₹2,875cr of liquid assets is not a demanding price for that quality.',
            '**Emcure and Marksans** are the next tier and I would own both. Emcure\'s position as the distribution partner of choice for Novo, Roche, Sanofi and MSD in India is a franchise that cannot be assembled quickly, and the market is discounting it for a gross margin dilution that is a mix effect rather than a deterioration. Marksans is the only company here that has found a defensible way to sell generics into the West, and I expect its H2 margin "miss" to be misread as a problem when it is simply the inventory buffer unwinding exactly as guided.',
            'I would **not** own the expensive-and-unproven cohort. Zota at 214x with losses, Orchid at 320x on a 1.7% return, Wockhardt at 90x on a single drug, Sakar at 71x before the ramp. Each may work. None of them offers protection if it does not, and this industry misses timetables for entirely innocent reasons.',
            'The two names I keep returning to and keep not buying are **Rubicon and JB Chem**. Rubicon is the best R&D engine in the sector and I would be a buyer 30% lower. JB is a superb franchise mid-way through a control change with guidance suspended, and I would rather pay more once the Torrent integration has proven it did not break the field force.',
            '**Sigachi is the one I would rule out entirely**, and I want the Committee to be clear this is a governance decision rather than a valuation one. Litigation against the chief executive, a quarter of promoter holding pledged and being invoked, a year\'s delay on the key project, an insurance recovery management admits will be haircut, and an acknowledged possibility of dilution — I do not need to form a view on MCC pricing to decline that.',
            'What would change my mind on the sector: a genuine acceleration in US generic pricing, which would make Strides and Alembic interesting on asset value alone; or confirmation that the 2028 tariff schedule will be enforced as written, which would immediately reprice the three companies here that already own US plants. I am watching both, and neither is in the price today.',
        ],
        bottomLine:
            'Buy Indian doctors\' prescribing habits, not American wholesalers\' purchase orders. On this list that means Ipca, Ajanta, Corona, Caplin, RPG and Jagsonpal — and it means declining roughly a third of the sector outright.',
    },

